[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3922329479","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112139#issuecomment-3922329479","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112139","id":3922329479,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pyf-H","user":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-18T18:01:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T18:01:16Z","body":"I have tested the MRP with the changes of this PR rebased on v4.7.dev.custom_build [8db94f7b5].\r\n\r\nWhen using `stretch_shrink = 1`, the game window and the remote view look the same:\r\n<img width=\"947\" height=\"363\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ecbc4901-b6e5-4009-854f-43f49e4c5add\" />\r\n\r\nWhen using `stretch_shrink = 2`, the game window and the remote view look different:\r\n<img width=\"937\" height=\"363\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4d003aa4-a77a-4a8d-922a-5ff1e50920a5\" />\r\n\r\nI assume, that this discrepancy between the display of the game window and the remote view is the bug, that you seek help for.\r\nSo my guess is, that you would like, that the remote view in the editor window looks like the content of the game window. Please tell me, if my assessment of the problem is correct.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3922329479/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3922520359","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112139#issuecomment-3922520359","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112139","id":3922520359,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pzOkn","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-18T18:42:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T18:43:20Z","body":"> I assume, that this discrepancy between the display of the game window and the remote view is the bug, that you seek help for.\r\n\r\nNo, this isn't a bug. This happens because cameras inside scenes aren't enabled while in the editor.\r\n\r\nThis is the main blocker for this PR, as per the OP:\r\n\r\n> Either zooming with the overridden camera or using the stretch_shrink feature of SubViewportContainer while there's a camera inside the SubViewport results in incorrect locations for clicking.\r\n\r\nTry clicking the sprites in those conditions, and you will see that won't be able to select them.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3922520359/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3974460947","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112139#issuecomment-3974460947","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112139","id":3974460947,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7s5XYT","user":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T18:38:45Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T18:43:32Z","body":"I wanted to give feedback about what I did in the meantime.\r\n\r\nI did an initial rewrite of the `_find_canvas_items_at_pos` function:\r\nhttps://github.com/Sauermann/godot/tree/find-canvas-items-at-pos-rewrite\r\n\r\nThis is still WIP and I haven't tested it yet, but I intend to continue with this.\r\n\r\nThere is one situation, for which I can't tell, what the expected behavior should be.\r\n\r\nConsider the setting, where I have a `SubViewportContainer` with child `SubViewport`, which contains `CanvasItem` nodes.\r\nIf I click on one of the `CanvasItem` nodes, I also click on the `SubViewportContainer`, becaust they are both at the same screen location.\r\nIn such a case, should the `SubViewportContainer` also be included in the list of clicked CanvasItems`.\r\nI can think of the following ways to handle this situation:\r\n1. `SubViewportContainer` is never added to the list, but all CanvasItems\r\n2. `SubViewportContainer` is always added to the list and also the CanvasItems\r\n3. `SubViewportContainer` is only added to the list, if no Child CanvasItems get selected by the mouse click\r\n4. `SubViewportContainer` is always added to the list but none of the CanvasItems\r\n\r\nPlease let me know, which variant makes the most sense. I would consider Number 2 to be the most sensible solution.\r\n\r\nEdit: I also noticed, that `res.order` stores references about the canvas layer. When dealing with multiple SubViewports, one has to consider an additional order based on the hierarchy of Viewports.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3974460947/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3974672665","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112139#issuecomment-3974672665","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112139","id":3974672665,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7s6LEZ","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T19:24:19Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T19:24:19Z","body":"*Everything* below the mouse must be added to the list.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3974672665/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4150730715","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112139#issuecomment-4150730715","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112139","id":4150730715,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73Zx_b","user":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/u